===Season format===
The regular season runs from the first weekend of September through the second weekend of December. Each Division 1 team plays a 14-game schedule (home-and-away against all division opponents, plus two cross-division games). The top four teams in Division 1 qualify for the playoffs.

The postseason consists of two rounds:
* '''Semifinal''': 1st vs. 4th, 2nd vs. 3rd (single elimination)
* '''Rice Bowl''': Semifinal winners (national championship)

The Rice Bowl is held on the second Saturday of January at a rotating neutral site. Recent venues include the Toyozawa Dome, Okami National Stadium, and the Aizawa Maritime Arena.

===Foreign player regulations===
The X-League permits each team to roster a maximum of four foreign (non-Sanese) players, with no more than two on the field simultaneously. The majority of foreign players come from [[Kaneda]] and [[Kazabune]], where Lurandian Football is the dominant gridiron code. The league also maintains a "Shendan exception" allowing one additional player from a [[Shendan Ocean]] nation without counting against the foreign quota, reflecting Okaiken's regional sporting ties.

